  <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px; padding-top: 8px">
    <div style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">03 · a sea of reviewers</div>
    <h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 52px; line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.01em">More reviewers than ever. Fewer comments worth acting on.</h2>
    <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body)">GitClear tracks a dozen AI review bots week by week. One spikes, another crashes, a new one arrives. Meanwhile the share of review comments that lead to a changed line has slid from about 18% to about 5% in under a year, humans included.</p>
    <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body)">Knowing which tools capture the useful ideas with the least noise is an ongoing problem. Adding another comment stream doesn't solve it. A reviewer who can see what actually changed does.</p>
    <div style="padding: 20px 22px; border-radius: 14px; background: var(--ink); color: var(--page); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
      <div style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 12px; color: #A8ADB8">Diff Digest's approach</div>
      <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5">Classify every line before you read it, sort files by how much they need a human, and answer your questions on demand, not in a pile of unsolicited comments.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
